[
  {"comment": "The threads query on modelled tapped holes (mitcad#436): a 30 x 30 x 12 block (Sketch1 F1, Extrude1 F2) with a modelled M6x1 6H hole through all at (15, 15) on its top face (Hole1 F3)."},
  {"cmd": "sketch.create"},
  {"cmd": "sketch.add_rectangle", "sketch": "F1", "corner": [0, 0], "width": 30, "height": 30},
  {"cmd": "add_feature", "def": {"type": "extrude",
    "profiles": [{"sketch": "F1", "region": "r{c1[c4,c2],c2[c1,c3],c3[c2,c4],c4[c3,c1]}"}],
    "extent": {"type": "distance", "distance": 12}, "operation": "new_body"}},
  {"cmd": "add_feature", "def": {"type": "hole",
    "placement": {"type": "face", "body": "F2.b0", "face": "F2:end(r{c1[c4,c2],c2[c1,c3],c3[c2,c4],c4[c3,c1]})",
                  "points": [[15, 15, 12]]},
    "diameter": 5, "extent": {"type": "through_all"},
    "thread": {"designation": "M6x1", "class": "6H", "modeled": true}}},
  {"expect": {"feature": "Hole1", "status": "ok"}},
  {"comment": "The bore is the minor diameter D1 = 4.9174682, so the crest lies on the wall, pieces of which stay: the thread runs over the wall, from the top (the wall's axis points into the material) to the bottom."},
  {"expect": {"body": "F2.b0", "has_face": "F3:hole0.wall"}},
  {"expect": {"body": "F2.b0", "has_face": "F3:thread(F3:hole0.wall)"}},
  {"expect": {"query": {"query": "threads"}, "result": [{"feature": "F3", "face": "F3:hole0.wall", "designation": "M6x1",
    "class": "6H", "modeled": true, "internal": true, "major_diameter": 6, "minor_diameter": 4.917468245269452,
    "radius": 2.458734122634726, "start": [15, 15, 12], "end": [15, 15, 0]}]}},

  {"comment": "A radial clearance of 0.1 puts the crest off the wall (D1 + 0.2), so no piece of the wall is left, and the hole made the wall in the same step: the thread is listed just the same, on the wall as the hole measured it before cutting the thread."},
  {"cmd": "edit_feature", "uid": "F3", "def": {"type": "hole",
